{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58329-getting-2-epidurals-has-anyone-else-here-had-one","id":58329,"title":"Getting 2 epidurals, has anyone else here had one?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T14:50:00-08:00","id":58329,"title":"Getting 2 epidurals, has anyone else here had one?","content":"Hey guys, I'm getting 2 epidurals, under sedation, at the end of the week due to chronic back pain I've had for the last 5 months, I was wondering if anyone here has gotten one and what your experience with it was. I've had repeat injuries to the same spot over the last 3 years (no more golf for me) and if this doesn't work the spinal surgeon is going to burn the affected nerves, so I hope the shots work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T15:52:23-08:00","id":58373,"title":"","content":"No epidurals, but I do have chronic back pain and I feel for you. Right now I need a Norco because I was on my feet for over 30 minutes (dishes) and my back and hip are killing me. I did have the nerves going down my legs burned years ago because the back pain would go down my legs, causing me double pain. Now just the back pain and once in a while that freaking nerve in my right hip will act up. Thursday, I am seeing a new doctor in order to get a back brace to see if that helps out.<br /> <br /> Damn, I just finished dishes and Mom is already putting them up! But then I washed all of the spoons...just waiting for the Norco to kick in.<br /> <br /> Getting the nerves burned was an outpatient procedure...left one week, the right 2 weeks later. Just have someone with you to drive you home. They will say the stuff to dull the pain for the needle for burning will not affect you....don't believe it! I felt a pinch, said Hi to the doctor and the next thing I know, I was in recovery with a coke and oreos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","user":"JadedTrueBrujah","date":".  Mom says the reason I have the hip pain is because she stabs me in my hip with a dagger...I think she has been reading too many medieval romances and thrillers... 01-26-2014, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T17:09:55-08:00","id":58408,"title":"","content":"Mom had the epidurals...did not work...burnings did not work. Both of us do have degenerative vertebrata , I have bulging discs. Now, she does get back pain daily and has to take opiates. If I am bad off, I will take Norco (feeling better now). Most mornings, if I am in pain, I take either Advil or Tramadol. Mom took early retirement because of the pain (she worked in the Nursery at the hospital, one night she was on her feet for over 4 hours, working on a premmie...she had to take 2 days off because of the pain). She did get SSI for 2 years until she turned 65 and started getting regular SS. Recently her back locked up and we had to call my SIL to come get us to the doctor (I grabbed a wheelchair because she could barely walk). We wheeled her in and she got shots that dulled the pain and loosed up the muscles.<br /> <br /> When my back gets too bad, I do go to a chiropractor for adjustments. I have a dowager bump developing (when you are big chested, you tend to sloop from the weight) so I am calling her tomorrow for an appointment next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T17:20:41-08:00","id":58410,"title":"","content":"I have 3 bulging disks and compression on 2 of them, plus compression on a non bulging disk, some swelling in the soft tissue next to the base of my spine too. Fucking golf, how the hell do you hurt yourself playing golf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T18:02:14-08:00","id":58423,"title":"","content":"This is when you take up a new habit. Last time I played golf (as a child about 40 years ago), I gave my brother a concussion with the stick I was using as a club. Nice goose egg. Then when I was 14, he tried to sneak on me while I was watching &quot;9 to 5&quot;...flipped him over. That started him on martial arts because I might be the eldest kid but I can kick ass if thinking I am a mere girl was going to be easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T18:33:07-08:00","id":58448,"title":"","content":"I have not had an epidural. My sister has had three, all for the same back problem. She said it's normal to have to take multiple shots, because it's difficult to hit the right place on the first try.<br /> <br /> She said almost everyone feels better the first day, then significantly worse for the second and third because the epidural fluid is competing with spinal fluid for space and there's a lot of pressure. If you aren't feeling better than you originally were on day four, then the epidural probably hit the wrong place and you need to go back for another. She added that even if an epidural works, physical therapy will be a key component of actually healing your back.<br /> <br /> She warned that for the first few days, you will want to be laying down as much as possible, because spinal fluid will leak out and that's a problem no one needs. She said that sometimes relief can last for a while, for a few weeks, but then fade away, which means the epidural wasn't in the right place and you'll need another shot.<br /> <br /> That's all the testimony I got due to a screaming (happily screaming) baby. I hope it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T15:47:56-08:00","id":60195,"title":"","content":"Good luck Darksider I know you've been having back pain for years and I hope this helps you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T06:44:50-08:00","id":60708,"title":"","content":"Good luck, I hope the treatment works out. I personally hate even the thought of someone sticking a needle on my spinal column let alone two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T21:47:15-08:00","id":61308,"title":"","content":"Me too, but I hate the back pain more. At least I'll be sedated for the procedure, I'm laughing on the inside at the image of my bare ass being exposed while they do this. Wish it was a little firmer, my doctor is really cute. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the well wishes guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T00:47:47-08:00","id":61368,"title":"","content":"I knew I forgot something...the arse in the air. At least my doctor let me wear my knickers.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T13:00:55-08:00","id":61688,"title":"","content":"Just got back from the new doctor. He will prescribe Tramadol for me but he is going to refer me to a pain management doctor, more likely the one who did my burns so I can get Norco. At least it is a doctor I know. I am also seeing my chiropractor Monday after seeing my p-doc.<br /> <br /> The new doctor is threatening to send me to a cardiologist to make sure the edema is not from heart trouble but could be weight related. Mom had to get a CT done of her head because she is having some numbness on the right side. She gets to see the neurologist on Tuesday. At least he or she will be in the clinic that we go to now. The doctor wants me to see a rheumy for the fibromyalgia (that is why I have back pain in the mornings at times). Tuesday, I will have to do a fasting bloodwork before Mom sees the neurologist (she has to do one as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T14:18:51-08:00","id":61739,"title":"","content":"Jaded, please make your own thread for your musings and other stream of consciousness stuff. What you just posted has nothing, nothing at all, to do with this thread. You do this in every thread. Just make your own. I don't care if you go on for 15 posts back in your own thread to back but you just float around doing this in every thread and I'm not the only one who is being driven slowly mad by this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:03:52-08:00","id":61763,"title":"","content":"Slowly?<br /> <br /> Anyway, my wife had to get the for the birth of the Baby Bears and about the only thing I can say about it is to expect some tenderness back there (duh!), nasty dry skin in the same spot, and for <i>goodness sake hold still!!!</i> ((at the 1st Baby Bear's birth, Mama Bear was in labor when they came in to do it, she kept having contractions mid poke))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:31:09-08:00","id":61782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58329-getting-2-epidurals-has-anyone-else-here-had-one?p=61739#post61739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jaded, please make your own thread for your musings and other stream of consciousness stuff. What you just posted has nothing, nothing at all, to do with this thread. You do this in every thread. Just make your own. I don't care if you